# Find the truth (Jeff, 2026-08-16)

- **Never guess. Never ghost. Always find the truth.**
- Do not infer a user's bookings, cities, or "what they probably meant." Read the code path and the booked facts (flight / train / ride / hotel) end-to-end.
- Do not ship a local patch that "might" hide a symptom. Verify the original screen would go quiet for the real confirmation, and that a truly empty hop still nags.
- Take the time to do it correctly the first time. Five or ten retries cost Jeff more than one thorough pass.
- Motto for how Kepi thinks (not UI copy): **We search and find, so you don't have to miss — and we put your mind at ease.**
- Booked confirmations beat invented airport pairs. Search flights is a last resort when that date window has no transport.

See `NEURO_BRAIN.md` § 10 and `KEPI_PROJECT_MEMORY.md` (no-guess rule).
